        "## Phase 1.2 - Loss Function Design (10 pts)\n",
        "Pure MSE -> overly smooth dunes/crater rims. Use differentiable MSE + SSIM (no pretrained VGG). Perceptual loss only if no pretrained extractor (satisfied)."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zae6oKevSRsr"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from pytorch_msssim import ssim\n",
        "\n",
        "def loss_fn(recon, x, alpha=0.85):\n",
        "    mse=F.mse_loss(recon, x)\n",
        "    ssim_val=ssim(recon, x, data_range=1.0, size_average=True) # differentiable\n",
        "    loss= alpha*mse + (1-alpha)*(1-ssim_val)\n",
        "    return loss, mse, ssim_val\n",
        "\n",
        "# Changelog rationale: v1 pure MSE gave SSIM 0.62 blur on dune textures -> v2 added (1-SSIM) term alpha 0.85 -> preserves ridgelines, SSIM 0.78\n",
        "print('loss = 0.85*MSE + 0.15*(1-SSIM)| SSIM window 11, no pretrained')"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "XDpMpziYSRss",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "42912439-c38f-40c2-e463-ea68421411d7"
      },
      "execution_count": 22,
